## Smart contract design

One contract, `MandateVault`, plus a mock stablecoin with a public `mint` for the demo. It is plain Solidity on Monad testnet, so standard Foundry or Hardhat tooling works.

```solidity
struct Mandate {
    address owner;
    address agent;          // the agent key allowed to call pay()
    address token;          // demo stablecoin
    uint128 budget;         // locked at creation
    uint128 spent;
    uint128 perPaymentCap;
    uint64  expiry;
    bytes32 purposeHash;    // keccak256 of the approved sentence + parsed JSON
    bool    closed;
}
mapping(uint256 => Mandate) public mandates;
mapping(uint256 => mapping(address => bool)) public payeeAllowed;
mapping(address => bool) public frozen;   // keyed by agent
```

| Function | Who calls it | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `createMandate(agent, token, budget, perPaymentCap, expiry, payees[], purposeHash)` | Owner | Pulls `budget` into escrow and emits `MandateCreated` |
| `pay(id, payee, amount, cartHash)` | Agent | Runs the checks. Passes: transfers and emits `PaymentMade`. Fails: emits `PaymentBlocked(reason)` and returns `false` without reverting |
| `close(id)` | Owner or agent | Refunds `budget - spent` to the owner and emits `MandateClosed` |
| `reclaimExpired(id)` | Anyone | After expiry, refunds the owner |
| `setFrozen(agent, bool)` | Owner | Panic button for every mandate that agent holds |
| `canPay(id, payee, amount)` | Anyone (view) | Pre-check that returns `(ok, reason)` for the MCP server and the store badge |

**Check order in `pay`:** the caller is the mandate's agent (otherwise revert, so strangers can't spam events), then not closed, not expired, agent not frozen, payee allowed, amount within the per-payment cap, and spent plus amount within budget.

**Reason codes:** `CLOSED`, `EXPIRED`, `FROZEN`, `PAYEE_NOT_ALLOWED`, `OVER_PAYMENT_CAP`, `OVER_BUDGET`.

**Why blocked payments don't revert:** a reverted transaction leaves no event. Emitting `PaymentBlocked` puts every stopped attack on-chain, where the leaderboard and the proof trail can read it.

